      "content": "it's strange to hear you say that. most people would be trying to argue for staying, but you're actually agreeing that an intentional exit is a valid way to reclaim autonomy. if the cost of living has become too high, you're essentially saying it's logical to just close the account. how do you differentiate between a \"rational\" exit and just giving in to despair?",
